<title>BELGIUM: Niinisto hopeful on EMU budget pact.</title>
<headline>Niinisto hopeful on EMU budget pact.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1996-12-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Finnish Finance Minister Sauli Niinisto said on Monday he believed the prospects for reaching an agreement on a European Union (EU) budget stability pact were &quot;better than expected&quot;.</p>
<p>Asked as he arrived for a meeting of EU finance ministers whether he believed they would reach a compromise on an EMU stability pact he said: &quot;I hope so. The situation is better than expected.&quot;  </p>
<p>He also said he believed that ministers would agree a new currency mechanism, the ERM 2, with 15 percent fluctuation bands.</p>
<p>The ERM 2 will limit the fluctuations of currencies from EU countries that do not immediately join the single currency.</p>
<p>&quot;I do belive there will be 15 percent bands,&quot; Niinisto said.</p>
</text>
